{
  "id": "tmux",
  "name": "tmux",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Development",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "WindowsTerminal.exe",
      "wt.exe",
      "mintty.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [],
    "window_title": [
      "tmux"
    ]
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tmux/tmux/master/tmux.1",
    "https://man.openbsd.org/tmux.1",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tmux/tmux/master/key-bindings.c"
  ],
  "note": "tmux itself has no exe/bundle - it's a program running inside a terminal emulator, so this profile only fires when a Windows terminal's window title contains \"tmux\" (set your pane/window title, e.g. `tmux rename-window tmux` or `set -g set-titles on`). Bindings are taken from the \"DEFAULT KEY BINDINGS\" section of tmux's own man page (tmux.1, upstream git master, dated 2026-09-03) and, for copy mode, the \"WINDOWS AND PANES\" section's copy-mode command table. Every top-level binding is prefix (Ctrl+B by default) then a key, encoded as a 2-step sequence. Copy-mode commands do not use the prefix; tmux keeps two separate copy-mode key tables selected by the `mode-keys` option (emacs is tmux's default) - vi bindings are under context \"Copy Mode (vi)\" and emacs bindings under \"Copy Mode\"; both are listed where the man page documents both. The man page groups \"M-1 to M-7\" (arrange panes in a preset layout) and \"g 1-4 / g Up,Down,Left,Right\" (move a floating pane to a corner/edge) under single collective entries without saying which number maps to which layout/corner; that specific order was cross-checked against tmux's own key-bindings.c defaults (same upstream repo) and is not otherwise documented in the man page prose. The Meta-resizes-as-well variant of the g-corner/edge bindings, and the M-1..M-9 \"repeat count\" bindings inside copy mode, require a following numeric prompt or aren't spelled out as distinct key sequences in the man page text, so they're omitted. The man page also lists `cursor-centre-vertical` with an `(emacs: C-l)` binding, but tmux's own key-bindings.c binds Ctrl+L only to `recentre-top-bottom` in the emacs copy-mode table (not to cursor-centre-vertical) - this looks like a stale/duplicated entry in the man page, so cursor-centre-vertical is listed here with no default key. A handful of bindings exist in tmux's current development source (key-bindings.c) but are not yet documented in the DEFAULT KEY BINDINGS man page section - toggle pane floating/tiled (@), customize-mode (C), spread panes evenly (E), switch to session (BTab), move the visible part of the window (Shift+Up/Down/Left/Right), and reset-follows-cursor (Delete) - these are left out per \"do not invent bindings\" beyond what the man page documents.",
